[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:47. A Thirsty Ghost]
[00:00.240]Passage 47 | 文章四十七
[00:02.430]A thirsty ghost. | 一只口渴的鬼。
[00:05.705]A public house which was recently bought by Mr. Ian Thomson | 伊恩·汤姆森先生最近买下了一家小酒店。
[00:11.795]is up for sale. | 现在又要出售了。
[00:13.935]Mr. Thomson is going to sell it because it is haunted. | 汤姆森先生之所以要卖掉它，是因为那里闹鬼。
[00:19.335]He told me that he could not go to sleep one night | 他告诉我，有一天晚上他无法入睡，
[00:23.410]because he heard a strange noise coming from the bar. | 因为他听到酒吧里传来一阵奇怪的响声。
[00:28.580]The next morning he found that the doors had been blocked by chairs | 第二天早晨，他发现门被椅子堵住了，
[00:34.585]and the furniture had been moved. | 家具也被搬动了。
[00:37.825]Though Mr. Thomson had turned the lights off before he went to bed, | 尽管汤姆森先生睡觉前关了灯，
[00:43.195]they were on in the morning. | 可早晨灯却是亮着的。
[00:45.995]He also said that he had found five empty whisky bottles | 他还说，他发现了5只空的威士忌酒瓶，
[00:51.650]which the ghost must have drunk the night before. | 肯定是那鬼头天晚上喝的。
[00:55.745]When I suggested that some villagers must have come in for a free drink, | 当我提出可能有些村民曾来这儿免费喝酒时，
[01:01.235]Mr. Thomson shook his head. | 汤姆森先生摇了摇头。
[01:04.415]The villagers have told him that they will not accept the inn | 村民们告诉他，他们不会接受那家小酒店，
[01:09.450]even if he gives it away. | 即使他白送给他们都不要。